+# Task 2: Create scripts/design-absorption-markers.sh
+
+- **Target files:** `scripts/design-absorption-markers.sh` (create), `tests/unit/test-design-absorption-markers.bats` (create)
+- **Dependencies:** none
+- **LOC estimate:** ~80
+- **Description:** A new context-free script `scripts/design-absorption-markers.sh <design-path>` greps the named `design.md` file for the 4 canonical absorption-marker patterns and prints the absorbed-goal redirect map to stdout, one entry per line, tab-separated (`<absorbed-ID>\t<absorbing-ID|"no-task">`). The 4 enumerated patterns are: heading-suffix `^## G\d+ — .+: (moot|absorbed by CD-\d+|already fixed)`; block-internal `\*\*Explicit non-goal\.\*\*`; acceptance-criterion `no separate v\d+\.\d+(\.\d+)? task ships under (the )?G\d+ ID`; and free-prose `deferred to v\d+\.\d+`. The script extracts the goal ID (e.g. `G3`) from each matched context and infers the absorbing ID from the heading-suffix form where present, emitting `"no-task"` for the three non-suffix forms. The map is a transient view computed on demand; no committed map artifact is written. The script exits 0 on success — including empty output for a marker-free `design.md` — and exits 1 when `<design-path>` is missing or unreadable. The companion bats test drives the script against a fixture `design.md` containing all 4 marker forms and asserts the expected map output, and against a marker-free fixture and asserts empty output. Dispatch order: test-writer first, implementer second (RED-verification gate between).
+- **Test expectations:**
+  - Running the script against a fixture `design.md` that contains one instance of each of the 4 marker patterns (heading-suffix, block-internal `**Explicit non-goal.**`, acceptance-criterion "no separate vN.N task ships under … ID", free-prose "deferred to vN.N") produces exactly 4 tab-separated map lines on stdout, each matching `<goal-ID>\t<absorbing-ID-or-no-task>`
+  - For a heading-suffix marker of the form `## GX — …: absorbed by CD-N`, the map entry is `GX\tCD-N`; for a heading-suffix of the form `## GX — …: moot` or `## GX — …: already fixed`, the map entry is `GX\tno-task`
+  - For each of the three non-suffix marker forms (`**Explicit non-goal.**`, acceptance-criterion, free-prose), the map entry for the goal block in which the marker appears is `<goal-ID>\tno-task`
+  - Running the script against a marker-free fixture `design.md` produces empty stdout and exits 0
+  - Running the script with a missing or unreadable `<design-path>` argument exits 1 and emits a diagnostic message to stderr; stdout is empty
+  - Running the script with no arguments exits 1 and emits a usage message to stderr
+  - Output lines are tab-separated (a literal tab character between columns), with no trailing whitespace; the map contains one entry per matched marker occurrence
+  - The script is executable (`chmod +x`) and has a `#!/usr/bin/env bash` shebang
