+# Task 12: Create tests/lint/test-bats-test-name-id-hygiene.bats permanent CI lint
+
+- **Target files:** `tests/lint/test-bats-test-name-id-hygiene.bats` (Create)
+- **Dependencies:** T11
+- **LOC estimate:** ~50
+- **Description:** Permanent CI gate that greps every `@test "..."` line across `tests/**/*.bats` and asserts no description string contains a `\[T\d+(-[a-z0-9]+)?\]` or `\bR\d+-F\d+\b` marker. Fail output lists each violation as `file:line: <offending string>`. A `# bats lint:no-id-hygiene` comment immediately above a `@test` line exempts that test from the check (carve-out for fixture strings used by the lint's own fail-direction test). Runs on every PR in CI on the post-sweep clean tree.
+
+**Dispatch ordering note (TDD):** Test-writer dispatches first (authoring failing tests against the unimplemented file), then the RED-verification gate runs, then the implementer dispatches to reach GREEN.
+
+## Test expectations
+
+- **Passes on clean tree:** Running the lint against the post-T11-swept `tests/**/*.bats` corpus exits 0 with no output.
+- **Fails on T-ID match:** A `@test` description containing `[T12]` causes the lint to exit non-zero and print the `file:line: <string>` diagnostic for that line.
+- **Fails on R-ID match:** A `@test` description containing `R1-F2` causes the lint to exit non-zero and print the `file:line: <string>` diagnostic for that line.
+- **Match anywhere in string:** A token embedded mid-description (e.g., `"checks [T18] handler path"`) is caught — regex is not anchored to start/end of the description.
+- **Carve-out exempts the line:** A `@test` line preceded immediately by `# bats lint:no-id-hygiene` is skipped even if its description contains a forbidden token; the lint exits 0 for that file.
+- **Carve-out is exact line:** A `# bats lint:no-id-hygiene` comment separated from its `@test` by a blank line or another line does NOT exempt the `@test` below it.
+- **Multi-violation output:** When multiple `@test` lines in multiple files fail, all violations are listed before the lint exits non-zero (no early bail on first match).
+- **Scope limited to description strings:** Forbidden tokens appearing only inside the test body (not in `@test "..."`) do not trigger the lint.
