+### T25: Create scripts/validate-stage-commit-parents.sh with --capture/--validate and bats unit test
+- **Phase:** 1
+- **Target files:**
+  - `scripts/validate-stage-commit-parents.sh` — Create
+  - `tests/unit/test-validate-stage-commit-parents.bats` — Create
+- **Dependencies:** none
+- **LOC estimate:** ~150
+- **Description:** `scripts/validate-stage-commit-parents.sh` implements a two-entrypoint
+  pre/post validation fence around the wave-dispatch `git merge --no-ff` call. The
+  `--capture` entrypoint runs pre-merge: reads `git rev-parse HEAD` as the
+  integration-base SHA and `git rev-parse refs/heads/<name>` for each `--task-branches`
+  entry, then writes both fields to a runtime sidecar at
+  `<artifact-dir>/reviews/implement/wave-state/wave-W<N>-expected-parents.txt`
+  (line-oriented format: `integration_base_sha=<SHA>` and `task_tip_shas=<sha1> <sha2>
+  ...`). The `--validate` entrypoint runs post-merge: reads the sidecar written by
+  `--capture` for the same wave, reads actual parents from `git log --format='%P' -n 1
+  <stage-commit>`, and checks (a) `actual_parents[0] == captured integration_base_sha`
+  and (b) `set(actual_parents[1:]) == set(captured task_tip_shas)`. On failure, exits 4
+  with the named diagnostic `stage-commit-parent-mismatch:` on stderr. Exit codes: 0
+  success, 2 argument failure, 3 git operation failure, 4 parent mismatch. The sidecar is
+  runtime-only and lives under the `reviews/` tree that G5's orchestration-boundary check
+  already excludes; `parallelization.md` is unchanged after the wave (symbolic-only
+  branch-map invariant per research Q11/Q12).
+
+## Test Expectations
+
+- **Correct parents → silent pass.** Fixture stage commit whose actual parents exactly
+  match the integration-base SHA (first position) and all task-tip SHAs → `--validate`
+  exits 0, no output on stderr — traces to G6 acceptance: "Fixture stage commit with
+  correct parents → validation passes silently, wave advances."
+- **Wrong first-parent → halt with diagnostic.** Fixture stage commit where actual
+  `parent[0]` is not the captured integration-base SHA (a different SHA placed first) →
+  `--validate` exits 4, stderr contains `stage-commit-parent-mismatch:` and names the
+  wrong first-parent SHA — traces to G6 acceptance: "correct task-tip set but
+  integration-base NOT in parent[0] position → validation halts naming the wrong
+  first-parent SHA."
+- **Missing task tip → halt with diagnostic.** Fixture stage commit where one expected
+  task-tip SHA is absent from actual parents → `--validate` exits 4, stderr contains
+  `stage-commit-parent-mismatch:` and names the missing tip SHA under `task tips missing:`
+  — traces to G6 acceptance: "one task tip missing from parent set → validation halts
+  naming the missing tip."
+- **Unexpected extra parent → halt with diagnostic.** Fixture stage commit whose actual
+  parents include an extra SHA not present in the captured task-tip set → `--validate`
+  exits 4, stderr contains `stage-commit-parent-mismatch:` and names the extra parent
+  under `unexpected parents present:` — traces to G6 acceptance: "unexpected extra parent
+  → validation halts naming the extra parent."
+- **Single-task wave → correct counting.** Fixture wave with one task branch: actual
+  parents are [integration-base, task-tip]; captured sidecar has one task_tip_shas entry
+  → `--validate` exits 0 when parents match, exits 4 when integration-base is absent from
+  `parent[0]` — traces to G6 acceptance: "Single-task fixture wave → integration-base
+  parent correctly counted; passes when present, halts when absent."
+- **Capture writes both fields; parallelization.md unchanged.** A fixture bats test
+  invokes `--capture`, then asserts the sidecar contains both `integration_base_sha=` and
+  `task_tip_shas=` fields with the correct SHA values, and that `parallelization.md` has
+  not been modified — traces to G6 acceptance: "capture step coverage: sidecar carries
+  both fields; parallelization.md is unchanged after the wave (symbolic-only branch-map
+  invariant)."
+- **Missing sidecar → argument/git failure exit.** Invoking `--validate` when no sidecar
+  exists for the specified wave → exits non-zero (exit 2 or 3) with a diagnostic on
+  stderr; does not silently pass — traces to G6 acceptance: named diagnostic on failure,
+  no silent pass.
