+### T37: Create scripts/measure-active-footprint.sh, run it against the trimmed tree, and write docs/qrspi/2026-06-04-v073-release/g9-footprint-report.md
+- **Phase:** 1
+- **Target files:**
+  - `scripts/measure-active-footprint.sh` — Create
+  - `docs/qrspi/2026-06-04-v073-release/g9-footprint-report.md` — Create
+- **Dependencies:** T32, T33, T34, T35, T36
+- **LOC estimate:** ~120
+- **Description:** Create `scripts/measure-active-footprint.sh`, which computes the
+  per-turn active-skill-prompt token footprint (using-qrspi + heaviest active skill +
+  `!cat`-resolved shared snippets) using a pinned deterministic tokenizer (default
+  `tiktoken:cl100k_base`). The script resolves `!cat skills/_shared/<topic>.md`
+  references transitively (a snippet that `!cat`s another snippet resolves recursively)
+  with cycle detection. Missing `!cat` targets halt with a named
+  `footprint-snippet-unresolvable:` diagnostic; detected cycles halt with
+  `footprint-snippet-cycle:` naming the cycle path. No silent skip in either case.
+  After the script is implemented and its tests pass, run it against the trimmed skill
+  tree (the post-T32–T36 state) and capture its stdout as the body of
+  `docs/qrspi/2026-06-04-v073-release/g9-footprint-report.md`. The report is the
+  final acceptance-gate evidence for G9's `< 30K tokens` floor. The task spec cites
+  R8 as the authority for any prose-density guidance applied in this task (per G9
+  Pass 3 requirement recorded in design.md § G9 Acceptance).
+
+- **Script interface** (from structure.md § G9):
+
+  ```
+  scripts/measure-active-footprint.sh [--skill <name>] [--all]
+                                      [--tokenizer <name>]
+  ```
+
+  | Flag | Semantics |
+  |---|---|
+  | `--skill <name>` | Measure with `<name>` as the active skill. Default: iterate every `skills/*/SKILL.md`, report the heaviest as the per-turn measurement. |
+  | `--all` | Append a per-skill TSV breakdown (`skill<TAB>tokens` rows) after the summary block. |
+  | `--tokenizer <name>` | Tokenizer to use. Default: `tiktoken:cl100k_base`. Accepted: `tiktoken:cl100k_base`, `tiktoken:o200k_base`. |
+
+  **Footprint formula (per skill):**
+  ```
+  tokens(skills/using-qrspi/SKILL.md)
+  + tokens(skills/<active-skill>/SKILL.md, after transitive !cat resolution)
+  ```
+
+  **`!cat` resolution semantics:** Lines matching
+  `^!cat\s+(skills/_shared/[^\s]+\.md)\s*$` in any SKILL.md body are substituted
+  in-place with the referenced file's contents before tokenization. Resolution is
+  transitive (recursive). A missing target halts with exit code 4 and a named
+  diagnostic. A cycle halts with exit code 5 and a named diagnostic.
+
+  **Stdout shape — single-skill / default-heaviest mode:**
+  ```
+  active_skill=<name>
+  tokenizer=<name>
+  total_tokens=<integer>
+  ```
+
+  `--all` appends a TSV block:
+  ```
+  skill<TAB>tokens
+  using-qrspi<TAB><n>
+  implement<TAB><n>
+  ...
+  ```
+
+  **Exit codes:**
+  | Code | Meaning |
+  |---|---|
+  | 0 | Success — count emitted. |
+  | 2 | Argument failure (unknown `--tokenizer`, or `--skill` not found). |
+  | 3 | `footprint-tokenizer-missing:` tokenizer binary/module not installed. |
+  | 4 | `footprint-snippet-unresolvable:` `!cat` target missing (named in diagnostic). |
+  | 5 | `footprint-snippet-cycle:` `!cat` cycle detected (cycle path named). |
+  | 6 | `footprint-skill-not-found:` `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` absent. |
+
+- **Test expectations:**
+  - Default invocation (no flags) against the trimmed tree exits 0, emits
+    `active_skill=`, `tokenizer=tiktoken:cl100k_base`, and `total_tokens=` lines, and
+    `total_tokens` value is ≤ 30000 — traces to G9 acceptance: "active-context token
+    measurement shows total per-turn footprint below 30K tokens for a typical session"
+  - `--skill implement` exits 0, `active_skill=implement` in stdout, `total_tokens`
+    reflects `using-qrspi/SKILL.md` + `implement/SKILL.md` with all `!cat` references
+    resolved transitively — traces to G9 acceptance: "footprint formula (per skill)"
+  - `--all` mode emits a TSV block with a `skill<TAB>tokens` header row followed by one
+    row per `skills/*/SKILL.md` found plus the `using-qrspi` row — traces to structure.md
+    § G9 `--all` stdout shape specification
+  - `--tokenizer tiktoken:o200k_base` exits 0 and records `tokenizer=tiktoken:o200k_base`
+    in stdout — traces to structure.md § G9 accepted tokenizer values
+  - `--tokenizer unknown-tokenizer` exits 2 with no count emitted — traces to exit code 2
+    (argument failure)
+  - `--skill nonexistent` exits 6 with `footprint-skill-not-found:` diagnostic on stderr —
+    traces to exit code 6 and structure.md diagnostic spec
+  - A `!cat` line referencing a missing snippet file halts with exit code 4 and
+    `footprint-snippet-unresolvable:` on stderr naming the consuming skill, the broken
+    reference line, and the missing path — traces to structure.md `!cat` resolution
+    semantics and G9 acceptance: "named diagnostics for unresolvable references"
+  - A `!cat` cycle (A→B→A) halts with exit code 5 and `footprint-snippet-cycle:` on
+    stderr naming the full cycle path — traces to structure.md cycle-detection spec
+  - When `tiktoken` is not installed, exits 3 with `footprint-tokenizer-missing:` diagnostic
+    on stderr and no count on stdout — traces to exit code 3
+  - `g9-footprint-report.md` exists, is non-empty, begins with `active_skill=` or a header
+    comment, and its `total_tokens=` value is ≤ 30000 — traces to G9 acceptance:
+    "output recorded at `docs/qrspi/2026-06-04-v073-release/g9-footprint-report.md`" and
+    design.md § G9 Acceptance footprint-measurement bullet
