+- **Description:** Author the G9 trim-audit lint gate. The file is a BATS grep audit that walks all active `skills/*/SKILL.md` files (excluding `skills/_shared/` and `.archive/`) and asserts zero matches for eight drift-token patterns — script-mechanic narrative restatements that Pass 2 of the G9 trim is required to remove. One `@test` per token yields actionable failure messages. A shared `_audit` helper runs `find … | xargs grep -En` and emits `file:line` diagnostics on any hit. The `setup()` block resolves `REPO_ROOT` via `git rev-parse`. Test names follow the `[G9] <token> — zero matches in active SKILL.md files` convention so CI output is self-documenting.
+- **Test expectations:**
+  - `tests/lint/test-skill-trim-audit.bats` is created and parseable by `bats --list` without error — traces to G9 acceptance: "Trim audit grep set confirmed."
+  - Each of the eight `@test` blocks passes (exits 0) when no drift token is present in any active SKILL.md — traces to G9 design §G9: "grep audit confirms zero matches."
+  - Each `@test` fails with a `file:line` diagnostic when its pattern appears in any active SKILL.md — traces to G9 acceptance: diagnostics identify the file and line of each violation.
+  - The corpus discovery excludes `skills/_shared/` and `.archive/` directories — shared snippets and archived skills are not subject to the drift-token ban.
+  - The patterns `sidecar.*schema`, `change_type:.*enum`, `verifier.*threshold`, and `third-party.*splitter` are matched with `-E` extended-regex semantics; `jobId`, `tmpfile`, `HEAD~1`, and `narrow\.broaden` match as fixed or anchored patterns under `-E` — traces to plan T38 row: "narrative restatements only; concrete script names in process-step calls are fine."
+  - The file declares `bats_require_minimum_version 1.5.0` (consistent with the G26/BW02 corpus requirement that all lint bats files carry the declaration).
